FTP accounts represent the access credentials for FTP (File Transfer Protocol) used to manage files on your web hosting plan.

USAGE:
  scw webhosting ftp-account <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create      Create a new FTP account within your hosting plan.
  delete      Delete a specific FTP account within your hosting plan.
  list        List all FTP accounts within your hosting plan.

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for ftp-account
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw webhosting ftp-account [command] --help" for more information about a command.
